            <ArticleTitle>Ovarian vein thrombosis associated with Crohn's disease: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>743-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A nonpuerperal patient with Crohn's disease and pelvic pain was incidently diagnosed with ovarian vein thrombosis. The patient's laboratory data were negative for an inherited hypercoagulopathy state. Ovarian vein thrombosis is a possible cause of pelvic pain in patients with Crohn's disease. Modern imaging technology has made it easier to diagnose the once-elusive ovarian vein thrombosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
